<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<model>
    <name>vacuum_dock</name>
    <version>1.0</version>
    <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
    <author>
        <name>Ilia O.</name>
        <email>iliao@kaia.ai</email>
    </author>
    <description>Auto-empty and mop-wash charging dock for oomwoo_one, 0.460 x 0.340 x 0.580 m, authored from primitives as the exact decomposition of a rounded prism: a 0.430 m wide core box spanning to the corner-tube centres, two 0.015 m side strips running from those centres out to the faces, and four 0.015 m radius corner tubes. Core and strips abut on the tube axis rather than overlapping, so the union has neither a gap at the corners nor two same-facing flat faces on a shared plane, which is what makes shading flicker. Strips and tubes run floor to top, so there is no seam between tower and bay walls. The bay is 0.400 wide where the tubes pinch in (20 mm either side of the 0.359 m bumper), 0.240 deep and 0.170 high (73 mm over the 0.097 m turret). A 0.100 m spacer block closes the back of the bay, sized laterally to the core box, for charging contacts to be mounted on later. The bay carries NO collision geometry - only the core, side strips and spacer do - so the robot can sit in it without the physics ejecting it.</description>
</model>
